<p>The privacy statute is the framework. The ICO publishes the guidance a UK business should read, not a blog. A Tuesday rule a trading desk can actually follow is narrower than a legal opinion: if you collected a person’s details to deliver a job, dropping those details into a consumer chat was probably not the purpose they expected. This page will not pretend to interpret a particular lawful basis, a transfer clause, or the automated-decision rules as amended. Ask counsel if the data is employee, health, children’s, or financial information beyond a redacted order status. The ICO’s own pages are the place to read what changed when the 2025 Act amended the UK GDPR. A paragraph here is not that reading.</p>
